    "name": "decide",
    "description": "Fast typed decisions from Laya, a ~421M-parameter decision model running locally on this machine (about 30-150 ms per call, no text generation, calibrated probabilities). Use it to classify, route, triage or score many items quickly: support tickets, log lines, commits, files, requests. Each question is {type, instructions, criteria}: type \"choice\" picks one key of criteria (an object of option -> description, at most ~20 options); \"noul\" gives P(yes) for a yes/no question (criteria optional, {\"true\": ..., \"false\": ...}); \"score\" picks a level from criteria (an array of level descriptions, low to high). Refer to the state in instructions with backticks, e.g. \"Which team should handle `message`?\". One call answers every question about one state; call once per item. Accuracy is that of a small untuned model: treat low-probability answers as uncertain and verify anything important yourself."
   }
